      "translations": {
        "en": "He said: 'Bring what you doubt in also.' He said: 'And I find Allah saying: The Day the Spirit and the angels stand in rows; they speak not except he whom the Most Merciful permits and says is correct; and He said: And they will be questioned and say: By Allah, our Lord, we were not polytheists; and He said: On the Day of Resurrection some of you will deny others and curse others; and He said: That is the truth, the contending of the people of the Fire; and He said: Do not quarrel before Me, for I had already sent the warning to you; and He said: We will seal their mouths, and their hands will speak to Us, and their feet will bear witness of what they used to earn. So one time He informs that they speak, and one time He informs that they do not speak except he whom the Most Merciful permits and says is correct, and one time He informs that the creation does not speak, and He says about their speech: By Allah, our Lord, we were not polytheists, and one time He informs that they quarrel. How is that, O Commander of the Faithful, and how should I not doubt what I hear?'"
